<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) 10-rupee stock rose 1.25 rupees to 30.80 on Saturday, a day after the government readjusted the excise tax on telephones.</p>
<p>Dealers at the Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) said the adjustment would likely boost PTCL's earnings. The stock, which rose 0.50 rupee during the unveiling of Friday's 1997/98 (July-June) budget, rose further on fresh buying on hope of its good results for the year ending on June 30, a dealer said. KSE has allowed special trading on its computerised system on Saturday, which is usually observed as a holiday.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
